{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"alias":"cherubic-content-woodpecker","creation_channel":"cli","description":"Escaped-bug analysis (ticket cranial-goodly-seahog) found ~4 regressions in a class current code-review criteria miss entirely: import/packaging resolution breakage that passes in-tree but fails under real import order / sys.path. Examples: cinderlike-faulty-yucker (helpers cannot import git adapter), spinal-grayish-perch (bare 'import alert_dedup' only resolves with scripts/ on sys.path), fibrous-fabulous-dungbeetle (preview lock test cannot import reconciler package), vapid-ferrous-weaverbird (monkeypatch breaks lazy provider import). Add a content-triggered import-integrity overlay (fires when a change moves/removes a module, edits sys.path, or reorders a lazy import / monkeypatch target), OR expand the existing deletion-impact overlay to cover import-graph breakage (not just dangling call sites). Advisory first; calibrate before blocking.","id":"8b86-fe08-16ea-4875","parent_id":"","priority":2,"tags":[],"ticket_type":"task","title":"Add code-review import-integrity criterion (catch import/packaging-resolution regressions)"},"env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","event_type":"CREATE","timestamp":1787070658446577001,"uuid":"a3d4d21e-fb19-4d3d-b2bd-42439d57fe08"}